}}

==Enemy==
Flying Ninja Cat has low range, slow movement and rapid, moderate damaging attacks with splash damage. She has one million health, being able to soak up many hits.

==Strategy==
In [[Ninja Awakens!]], the support is light enough that you can win using only 3-4 meatshields (including [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Macho Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]]) and a bunch of long-ranged attackers (e.g., [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]]). Otherwise, use [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating cats]] to deal with this enemy. [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako Cat]] is great here, as she can tank the damage and weaken the Ninja. [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] is another great unit because she outranges Flying Ninja Cat by 10, has a relatively short cooldown and can Survive a lethal strike. Just protect and spam her and the Ninja is killed in no time. An alternative method is stacking [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necromancer Cats]], though [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] is not as effective due to Flying Ninja already being relatively slow. The True Form of Necromancer Cat, Necro-Dancer Cat, is even more effective thanks to its higher standing range and higher freeze duration, which is especially important in [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 22|Floor]] [[Infernal Tower/Floor 22|22]], as the high magnification Flying Ninja appears with will quickly kill most units scarily quick.

